Sometimes you'll be able to identify mimics (if they mimic objects 
that don't belong there, even stairs or "]"). If you do, then don't 
attack it, take care not to bump into or search on the spaces around 
it. Instead you might let your pet attack it.

If you absolutely want or need to fight it, you might try to remove 
all breakable items before you shoot it (I agree that this is fairly 
impractical in potions shops, though). You also could lure it out of 
the shop.

Others have pointed to "Elbereth" in the case of large/giant mimics. 
Small mimics can't grab you, but still deal out enough damage to be 
dangerous. Teleporting them away is a bad idea in a shop, as it will 
also teleport the goodies they're sitting on. Teleporting *yourself* 
will help, though, if you don't have unpaid items. 

If you've broken something, and don't have enough money to pay the 
damage, you might try selling (high-value magical) stuff that you 
possess. Sometimes it might just be enough to pay the bill, and you 
can let your pet steal it back afterwards.

Just for completeness: Other ways to anger the shopkeeper (other than 
attacking him) are kicking down his door, digging into or out of his 
shop, stealing something (also by involuntarily teleporting out of the 
shop) or even zapping him with a non-attack wand like speed. 
He will want payment for using up anything he owns. This includes e.g.
reading spellbooks (there's a YAFM for this).

Note: If you tend to play characters with the same name, and you load 
a bones level, it might happen that the shopkeeper is angry at you 
because he "remembers" you (= your name) from another character (the 
one that left the bones) that stole from him.

